cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite the associated paper and this software bundle."
title: "1+3 covariant CMB anisotropies: analytical reproducibility software"
type: software
# Tracks the tag that exists, not the one being prepared. GitHub's "Cite this
# repository" and Zenodo both read this field, so a version here that has not
# been released asserts a release that cannot be fetched.
version: "1.2.0"
# Stamped by scripts/bump_release.py together with the version above, so the
# two cannot disagree about which release this file describes.
date-released: 2026-10-16
authors:
  - family-names: Gebbie
    given-names: Tim
doi: "10.25375/uct.34069509"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  An independent Python reconstruction, from first 1+3 covariant principles, of
  the almost-Friedmann-Lemaitre results of Gebbie, Dunsby & Ellis, Annals of
  Physics 282, 321 (2000). Analytical release; no empirical data are required.
preferred-citation:
  type: article
  # **Transcribed from the Zenodo record, not from decision S17.** The record
  # prints `CMBR`; S17 fixed `CMB`. A citation reproduces the title of the
  # thing it points at or it does not resolve for a reader, so this field
  # follows the artefact. The discrepancy is finding T-84 and is the PI's to
  # settle -- changing it the other way means a new Zenodo version.
  title: "Frame covariance of CMBR lensing in the exact 1+3 covariant radiation hierarchy"
  authors:
    - family-names: Gebbie
      given-names: Tim
      orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-4061-2621"
      affiliation: "University of Cape Town"
  year: 2026
  month: 10
  # Version DOI, read off the record. Zenodo's concept DOI is not exposed on
  # this record (Versions list empty), so it cannot be cited here yet.
  doi: "10.5281/zenodo.23475234"
  url: "https://zenodo.org/records/23475234"
  version: "v1.1.6"
  license: CC-BY-4.0
  notes: "Preprint, Zenodo, 19 October 2026. The arXiv identifier is assigned on submission and is filled at manuscript freeze (acceptance criterion 6); it is additional to this DOI, not a replacement for it."
keywords:
  - cosmic microwave background
  - 1+3 covariant formalism
  - multipole hierarchy
  - reproducibility
  - CMB lensing
  - frame covariance
